  "word_count": 780,
  "body_markdown": "(310)-481-0111\n\nDental Implants\n\nDental Implant Surgery\n\nAll-on-4® Dental Implants\n\nHybrid Fixed Detachable Denture\n\nZirconia Fixed Bridge\n\nImplant Supported Dentures\n\nRobotic Surgery\n\nCost & Compare\n\nWhat To Expect\n\nFAQ\n\nAesthetic Dentistry\n\nCosmetic Dentistry\n\nPorcelain Veneers & Lumineers\n\nInvisalign\n\nTeeth Whitening\n\nSmile Makeover\n\nServices\n\nIV Sedation\n\nBone Grafting\n\nRidge Augmentation\n\nSinus Augmentation\n\nTooth Extractions\n\nGeneral Dentistry\n\nPeriodontics\n\nConditions We Treat\n\nMissing Teeth\n\nBone Loss\n\nFailing Dental Implants\n\nLoose Dentures\n\nPatient Center\n\nInsurance & Financing\n\nOur Facility\n\nPatient Stories\n\nBefore & After Photos\n\nWho We Are\n\nCommitment To Excellence\n\nMeet Dr. Tony Barriere\n\nMeet The Team\n\nVideo Library\n\nBlog\n\nContact Us\n\nPatient Portal\n\nNew Patients\n\nCurrent Patients\n\n\n## Does Anything Happen To My Jawbone If I Don’t Immediately Replace My Missing Teeth With Dental Implants?\n\n\nAugust 14, 2023\n\n\n#### Share This Post\n\n\nShare on facebook\n\nShare on linkedin\n\nShare on twitter\n\nShare on email\n\nDental implants in Los Angeles, FL, are a gold standard tooth replacement option that are surgically placed in a patient’s jawbone. A dental implant post is designed to act like a natural tooth root, giving patients a permanent and stable new smile.\n\nWhen people don’t replace their missing teeth with restorative dental implants, their oral health and facial structure could be negatively affected. Continue reading to learn more about what could happen to the jawbone if missing teeth aren’t immediately replaced with dental implants.\n\n\n## What Happens To The Jawbone If Missing Teeth Aren’t immediately Replaced With Dental Implants In Los Angeles, FL\n\n\nIf people don’t replace their missing teeth with dental implants, then the bone in their jaw could shrink over time. This is known as jawbone resorption and it can cause functional problems, such as having difficulty chewing and speaking properly. Not replacing missing teeth can also lead to a sunken-in facial appearance and an altered bite.\n\nThis is why people should replace their missing teeth with dental implants. Dental implants are surgically placed into the jawbone, where they act like artificial roots that stimulate the jawbone and become a permanent part of the patient’s mouth. Replacing missing teeth with dental implants is essential for maintaining healthy jawbone structure and function.\n\n\n## How Are My Missing Teeth Replaced With Dental Implants In Los Angeles, FL?\n\n\nBecause every person’s smile is unique, dental implant procedures are customized to each patient’s specific smile. After the patient’s dental implant procedure is planned out in the consultation, the doctor will strategically and precisely place the dental implants into their jawbone.\n\nThe dental implants can then heal and integrate with the patient’s jawbone for several months. As the dental implants are fusing with the patient’s jawbone, a temporary crown or prosthesis can be placed on the dental implants so the patient can have a functioning and aesthetically pleasing smile while they wait for their final one.\n\nWhen the final prosthesis is ready, it will be securely attached to the dental implants. With dental implants, patients will be able to eat, speak, and smile for years to come.\n\n\n## See Us Now So We Can Replace Your Missing Teeth With Dental Implants\n\n\nDental implants are a secure and comfortable tooth replacement option. No matter how many teeth you are missing, dental implants will give you the functional, beautiful, and healthy new smile you need and deserve.\n\nWhy wait to improve your smile with us? Get in contact with our doctors, Dr. Tony Barriere, and our exceptional team at our dental office to schedule an appointment today!\n\nPrevPreviousAfter My Smile Has Healed, How Is The Final Prosthesis Placed?\n\nNextAre There Factors That Determine Which Type Of Dental Implant Procedure I Can Get Treated With?Next\n\n\n#### More To Explore\n\n\n\n### Are There Factors That Determine Which Type Of Dental Implant Procedure I Can Get Treated With?\n\n\nDental implants in Los Angeles, FL, are a safe and effective way to replace missing or damaged teeth. They are\n\nRead More »\n\nAugust 20, 2023\n\n\n### Does Anything Happen To My Jawbone If I Don’t Immediately Replace My Missing Teeth With Dental Implants?\n\n\n\n## You Are Welcome Here.\n\n\nSchedule your consultation today.\n\nCall Now\n\nFacebook Instagram Youtube Yelp Google\n\n\n#### Contact Us\n\n\nAddress:\n\n12301 Wilshire Blvd Suite 205,\n\nLos Angeles, CA 90025\n\n(310) 481-0111\n\n\n#### Hours\n\n\nMonday: 9:00am – 5:00pm\n\nTuesday: 9:00am – 5:00pm\n\nWednesday: 9:00am – 5:00pm\n\nThursday: 9:00am – 5:00pm\n\nFriday: 9:00am – 5:00pm\n\nSaturday: Closed\n\nSunday: Closed\n\n\n#### Services\n\n\n\n#### About Us\n\n\nPrivacy Policy\n\nDental Website by Progressive Dental Marketing",
